    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d434">

                <pb facs="0525" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.51/1727: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-02-09T21:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                                1927—9 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 10—12:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>38. Rene Keilhauer of Hebard Company<anchor n="35" xml:id="d434-f1"/> who arrived
                    today has consulted me about a loan not to exceed $300,000 which he contemplates
                    offering the Government, half of the proceeds or at least $100,000 to be used to
                    continue street pavement by his [company?]. Loan to be secured by Nicaraguan
                    Government increases reported in my telegram of January 31, 4 p.m.<anchor n="36"
                        xml:id="d434-f2"/> Please advise whether the Department sees any objection
                    to this loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d434-f1" n="35" xml:id="d434-f1-content">
                <p>R. W. Hebard and Company, engineers and contractors, of New York, N. Y.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d434-f2" n="36" xml:id="d434-f2-content">
